I briefly considered recommending `git config
merge.conflictstyle zdiff3` at the top of the session with an unset
at the end — it's less typing per command. But it's a two-step
ceremony that's easy to forget to clean up, and `git -c` is explicit
at each callsite. The `-c` form also matches the existing pattern in
the pitfalls section (`git -c rerere.enabled=false merge ...`), so it
reads consistently throughout.

The version is a patch bump. The skill's behaviour is otherwise
identical — zdiff3 just changes how conflict markers are rendered, not
the strategy or any step in the algorithm.
